{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1954 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "6d22a527dfcd77a2d979fe174327184883b0bd33d23d17949319a1359ddb3aad" :edb/db-before-t 1953 :edb/db-after-t 1954 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535266 50 #inst "2026-10-08T20:52:48.516Z" 13194139535266 true] [17592186091999 1100 "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x+2)^2}{18} - \\dfrac{(y+7)^2}{32} = 1$." 13194139535266 false] [17592186091999 1100 "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x+2)^2}{18} - \\dfrac{(y+7)^2}{32} = 1.$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186091999 1145 "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^2}{a^2} - \\frac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}(x-h)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n(h,k) = (-2,-7),\\qquad a=\\sqrt{18} = 3\\sqrt{2}, \\qquad b=\\sqrt{32} = 4\\sqrt{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny + 7 &= ± (\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{3\\sqrt{2}})(x + 2) \\\\\ny + 7 &= ± \\frac{4}{3}(x + 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535266 false] [17592186091999 1145 "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^2}{a^2} - \\frac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k) = (-2,-7),\\qquad a=\\sqrt{18} = 3\\sqrt{2}, \\qquad b=\\sqrt{32} = 4\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+7 & =\\pm (\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{3\\sqrt{2}})(x+2) \\\\ y+7 & =\\pm \\frac{4}{3}(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186092071 1100 "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $9x^2 - y^2 - 36 x - 2y + 26 = 0$." 13194139535266 false] [17592186092071 1100 "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $9x^2 - y^2 - 36 x - 2y + 26 = 0.$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186092071 1145 "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9x^{2} - y^{2} - 36x - 2y + 26 &= 0 \\\\\n9x^{2} - 36x - y^{2} - 2y + 26 &= 0 \\\\\n9[x^{2} - 4x] - [y^{2} + 2y] + 26 &= 0 \\\\\n9[(x - 2)^{2} - 4] - [(y + 1)^{2} - 1] + 26 &= 0 \\\\\n9(x - 2)^{2} - 36 - (y + 1)^{2} + 1 + 26 &= 0 \\\\\n9(x - 2)^{2} - (y + 1)^{2} &= -26 - 1 + 36 \\\\\n9(x - 2)^{2} - (y + 1)^{2} &= 9 \\\\\n&= (x - 2)^{2} - ((y + 1)^{2})/(9) = 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe asymptotes of the horizontal hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{b^2} = 1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\ny-k = \\pm\\dfrac{b}{a}(x-h)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nh = 2, \\qquad k = -1, \\qquad a = \\sqrt{1} = 1,\\qquad b = \\sqrt{9} = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny + 1 &= ± 3(x - 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535266 false] [17592186092071 1145 "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-36x-2y+26 & =0 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-36x-{y}^{2}-2y+26 & =0 \\\\ 9[{x}^{2}-4x]-[{y}^{2}+2y]+26 & =0 \\\\ 9[(x-2)^{2}-4]-[(y+1)^{2}-1]+26 & =0 \\\\ 9(x-2)^{2}-36-(y+1)^{2}+1+26 & =0 \\\\ 9(x-2)^{2}-(y+1)^{2} & =-26-1+36 \\\\ 9(x-2)^{2}-(y+1)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{9}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe asymptotes of the horizontal hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{b^2} = 1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\ny-k = \\pm\\dfrac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nh = 2, \\qquad k = -1, \\qquad a = \\sqrt{1} = 1,\\qquad b = \\sqrt{9} = 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+1 & =\\pm 3(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186092072 1145 "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2} = 1\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k = \\pm\\dfrac{a}{b}(x-h)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\na = \\sqrt{16} = 4, \\qquad b = \\sqrt{9} = 3, \\qquad h = -3, \\qquad k = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - 1 &= ± \\frac{4}{3}(x - (-3)) \\\\\ny - 1 &= ± \\frac{4}{3}(x + 3)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535266 false] [17592186092072 1145 "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2} = 1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k = \\pm\\dfrac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na = \\sqrt{16} = 4, \\qquad b = \\sqrt{9} = 3, \\qquad h = -3, \\qquad k = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-1 & =\\pm \\frac{4}{3}(x-(-3)) \\\\ y-1 & =\\pm \\frac{4}{3}(x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186092073 1100 "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $y^2 - x^2 - 2y = 0$." 13194139535266 false] [17592186092073 1100 "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $y^2 - x^2 - 2y = 0.$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186092073 1145 "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{2} - x^{2} - 2y &= 0 \\\\\n(y^{2} - 2y) - x^{2} &= 0 \\\\\n(y - 1)^{2} - 1 - x^{2} &= 0 \\\\\n(y - 1)^{2} - x^{2} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe asymptotes of the vertical hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2} = 1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\dfrac{a}{b}(x-h)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n(h,k) = (0,1), \\qquad a = \\sqrt{1} = 1, \\qquad b= \\sqrt{1} = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - 1 &= ± x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535266 false] [17592186092073 1145 "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-2y & =0 \\\\ ({y}^{2}-2y)-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (y-1)^{2}-1-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (y-1)^{2}-{x}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe asymptotes of the vertical hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2} = 1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\dfrac{a}{b}(x-h) .\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k) = (0,1), \\qquad a = \\sqrt{1} = 1, \\qquad b= \\sqrt{1} = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-1 & =\\pm x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186092157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340718 13194139535266 true] [17592186092157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340746 13194139535266 true] [17592186092157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340760 13194139535266 true] [17592186092157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340763 13194139535266 true] [17592186092157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340798 13194139535266 true] [17592186092224 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340725 13194139535266 true] [17592186092224 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340769 13194139535266 true] [17592186092224 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340812 13194139535266 true] [17592186092225 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340711 13194139535266 true] [17592186092225 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340739 13194139535266 true] [17592186092225 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340766 13194139535266 true] [17592186092225 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340791 13194139535266 true] [17592186092225 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340805 13194139535266 true] [17592186092226 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340732 13194139535266 true] [17592186092226 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340753 13194139535266 true] [17592186092226 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340773 13194139535266 true] [17592186092226 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340779 13194139535266 true] [17592186092226 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340784 13194139535266 true] [17592186092528 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535266 true] [17592186092528 1100 "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $x^{2} - y^{2} + 8x + 7 = 0$." 13194139535266 false] [17592186092528 1100 "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+8x+7=0.$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186092528 1145 "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+8x+7 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+8x-{y}^{2}+7 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-16-{y}^{2}+7 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-{y}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-{y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(-4,0),\\,a=\\sqrt{9}=3,\\,b=\\sqrt{9}=3.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\ny=\\pm (x+4).\n$$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186092780 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535266 true] [17592186092780 1100 "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $16x^{2} - y^{2} - 64x - 2y + 47 = 0$." 13194139535266 false] [17592186092780 1100 "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $16{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-64x-2y+47=0.$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186092780 1145 "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-64x-2y+47 & =0 \\\\ (16{x}^{2}-64x)+(-{y}^{2}-2y)+47 & =0 \\\\ 16[{x}^{2}-4x]-[{y}^{2}+2y]+47 & =0 \\\\ 16[(x-2)^{2}-4]-[(y+1)^{2}-1]+47 & =0 \\\\ 16(x-2)^{2}-64-(y+1)^{2}+1+47 & =0 \\\\ 16(x-2)^{2}-(y+1)^{2} & =64-1-47 \\\\ 16(x-2)^{2}-(y+1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{16(x-2)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{16}{16} \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{1}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nh=2,\\,k=-1,\\,a=\\sqrt{1}=1,\\,b=\\sqrt{16}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+1 & =\\pm \\frac{4}{1}(x-2) \\\\  & =\\pm 4(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186340711 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340712 13194139535266 true] [17592186340711 1089 "q-10470" 13194139535266 true] [17592186340711 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535266 true] [17592186340711 1100 "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{25}-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}=1.$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186340711 1113 #uuid "df144c9c-31f2-594e-958f-a4bf1a0938ce" 13194139535266 true] [17592186340711 1145 "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{25}=5,\\,b=\\sqrt{9}=3,\\,h=2,\\,k=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\ny-2=\\pm \\frac{5}{3}(x-2).\n$$" 13194139535266 true] [17592186340712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340713 13194139535266 true] [17592186340712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340714 13194139535266 true] [17592186340712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340715 13194139535266 true] [17592186340712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340716 13194139535266 true] [17592186340712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340717 13194139535266 true] [17592186340712 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535266 true] [17592186340712 1041 "selection" 13194139535266 true] [17592186340712 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340715 13194139535266 true] [17592186340712 1110 #uuid "0f21e628-4d04-5de9-afab-10e1fce64c9a" 13194139535266 true] [17592186340713 1034 "y-2=\\pm \\frac{9}{5}(x-2)" 13194139535266 true] [17592186340713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535266 true] [17592186340713 1111 #uuid "ac20d2f9-ef95-549c-b8c7-5cfede04d451" 13194139535266 true] [17592186340714 1034 "y+2=\\pm \\frac{3}{5}(x+2)" 13194139535266 true] [17592186340714 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535266 true] [175